 ## Overview
-World to UVW Normalization maps arbitrary 3D world coordinates into the normalized $[0, 1]$ range of a voxel grid, enabling consistent indexing and texture sampling regardless of the scene's physical scale or origin. It differs from [Coordinate Space Conversion](1785-coordinate-space-conversion.md) by explicitly handling the discrete voxel grid boundaries and dimensionality, and from [Texture Coordinate Conversion](3581-texture-coordinate-conversion.md) by operating at the grid indexing level rather than applying shader-specific offsets like Y-flips or centering adjustments.
